                'excerpt'        => 'Looking for the perfect gold ring? From delicate everyday bands to statement cocktail rings, we have curated the best gold ring designs for women in India across every budget and occasion.',
                'content'        => '<h2>Why Every Woman Needs at Least One Gold Ring</h2><p>A gold ring is more than jewellery — it is a statement of personal style, a mark of tradition, and often the first piece of fine jewellery a woman buys for herself. Whether you prefer a minimalist band for daily wear or an ornate temple-design ring for festivals, gold rings remain the most versatile jewellery investment in India.</p><h2>Understanding Gold Purity for Rings</h2><p>Before choosing a design, understand what you are buying:</p><ul><li><strong>24K gold (99.9% pure):</strong> Too soft for rings. Beautiful colour but scratches and bends easily.</li><li><strong>22K gold (91.6% pure):</strong> The Indian standard for jewellery. Rich yellow colour with enough durability for daily wear. Most traditional rings are 22K.</li><li><strong>18K gold (75% pure):</strong> Harder and more durable. Slightly lighter yellow. Ideal for rings with gemstone settings — the harder metal holds stones more securely.</li><li><strong>14K gold (58.5% pure):</strong> Most durable option. Popular for everyday western-style rings. Rose gold and white gold rings are often 14K or 18K.</li></ul><h2>Top Gold Ring Styles for 2026</h2><h3>1. Minimalist Bands (₹8,000 - ₹15,000)</h3><p>Thin, sleek gold bands are the biggest trend for everyday wear. A simple 2mm 22K gold band pairs with everything — ethnic or western. Stack two or three on one finger for a contemporary look. These are lightweight (1.5-3 grams) and perfect for women who work with their hands.</p><h3>2. Temple & Traditional Designs (₹15,000 - ₹35,000)</h3><p>Inspired by South Indian temple architecture, these rings feature intricate carvings of deities, lotus motifs, and paisley patterns. They are heavier (4-7 grams) and make a bold statement at pujas, weddings, and festivals. Look for antique-finish options for a vintage feel.</p><h3>3. Cocktail Rings (₹20,000 - ₹50,000)</h3><p>Large, eye-catching rings with coloured gemstones or bold geometric patterns. These are conversation starters — meant for parties, receptions, and evenings out. Many feature a combination of gold with kundan, polki, or meenakari work.</p><h3>4. Stackable Rings (₹6,000 - ₹12,000 each)</h3><p>Mix and match thin bands in yellow gold, rose gold, and white gold. Wear them together for a trendy layered look, or separately as subtle everyday pieces. This is the best way to build a ring collection over time.</p><h2>How to Choose the Right Gold Ring</h2><p><strong>For daily wear:</strong> Choose 18K or 14K gold in a low-profile design that will not snag on clothes. Comfort-fit bands with rounded inner edges are best for all-day wear.<br><strong>For occasions:</strong> Go bold with 22K gold. Heavier rings with detailed craftsmanship make a statement at weddings and celebrations.<br><strong>For gifting:</strong> Personalised rings with initials or birthstones add sentimental value. A gold ring in a velvet box never fails to impress.</p><blockquote>A gold ring is the one piece of jewellery you will reach for every single day. Choose one that reflects your personality and feels comfortable on your finger. Explore our curated gold ring collection at Trendimus and find your perfect match.</blockquote>',
