                'tags'           => ['gold chain', 'gold chain designs', 'gold chain for men', 'gold chain for women', 'gold chain weight', '22kt gold chain', 'hallmark gold chain'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-gold-chain.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'Gold chains are the foundation of any jewellery collection. This guide covers the most popular chain styles in India, how to choose the right weight and length, and current prices for 22K and 18K gold chains.',
                'content'        => '<h2>The Gold Chain: India\'s Most Worn Jewellery Piece</h2><p>From a newborn\'s first black-beaded chain to a grandmother\'s thick rope chain — gold chains are woven into Indian life. They are worn daily, gifted on auspicious occasions, and passed down through generations. Whether you are buying your first chain or adding to an existing collection, understanding chain styles, weights, and lengths makes all the difference.</p><h2>Popular Gold Chain Styles in India</h2><h3>For Women</h3><ul><li><strong>Box Chain:</strong> Clean, square links. Lightweight and elegant. Perfect for pendants. (2-5 grams)</li><li><strong>Rope Chain:</strong> Twisted links that catch light beautifully. The classic Indian chain. (5-15 grams)</li><li><strong>Singapore Chain:</strong> Flat, twisted links that sparkle with every movement. Very feminine. (3-8 grams)</li><li><strong>Bismark Chain:</strong> Interlocking links that lie flat against the skin. A modern favourite. (8-20 grams)</li><li><strong>Popcorn Chain:</strong> Textured, hollow links that look heavy but are lightweight. Great value. (4-8 grams)</li></ul><h3>For Men</h3><ul><li><strong>Figaro Chain:</strong> Alternating short and long links. The most popular men\'s chain worldwide. (15-40 grams)</li><li><strong>Cuban Link Chain:</strong> Thick, interlocking links. Bold and masculine. A statement piece. (20-60 grams)</li><li><strong>Flat Chain:</strong> Wide, flat links that sit flush on the chest. Comfortable under shirts. (10-30 grams)</li><li><strong>Franco Chain:</strong> V-shaped links woven together. Strong, durable, and kink-resistant. (15-35 grams)</li></ul><h2>Choosing the Right Chain Length</h2><p>Chain length changes the entire look:</p><ul><li><strong>16 inches (choker):</strong> Sits at the base of the neck. Best for women with slender necks. Pairs with traditional sarees.</li><li><strong>18 inches (princess):</strong> Falls just below the collarbone. The most popular length for women. Works with everything.</li><li><strong>20 inches (matinee):</strong> Most popular for men. Sits at the upper chest. Versatile and comfortable.</li><li><strong>22-24 inches:</strong> Falls mid-chest. Best for men who want the chain visible over t-shirts and kurtas.</li></ul><h2>Understanding Chain Weight & Pricing</h2><p>Gold chain price = Gold rate per gram x Weight in grams + Making charges (8-25%)</p><p>A 10-gram 22K gold chain at today\'s rate of approximately ₹6,800 per gram would cost around ₹68,000 + making charges of ₹5,000-₹17,000, totalling ₹73,000-₹85,000. Machine-made chains have lower making charges (8-12%) while handcrafted chains cost more (15-25%) but offer unique artistry.</p><h3>How to Save on Making Charges</h3><ul><li>Buy during festive sales — Dhanteras, Akshaya Tritiya, and Diwali often have reduced making charges</li><li>Choose machine-made chains for everyday wear</li><li>Compare making charges across jewellers — they vary significantly</li><li>Look for exchange offers if you have old gold to trade in</li></ul><blockquote>A gold chain is an investment you wear every day. Choose the right style for your personality, the right weight for your budget, and always insist on BIS hallmark. Browse our gold chain collection at Trendimus.</blockquote>',
