                'tags'           => ['gold earrings', 'jhumka designs', 'gold studs', 'gold hoops', 'earring designs 2026', 'traditional gold earrings', 'lightweight gold earrings'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-gold-earrings.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'From classic jhumkas to modern hoops, gold earrings complete every look. Explore the top gold earring designs trending in India in 2026, with tips on choosing the right style for your face shape.',
                'content'        => '<h2>Gold Earrings: The Jewellery You Wear Every Single Day</h2><p>Earrings are often the first piece of jewellery we put on and the last we take off. In India, gold earrings hold special significance — from a baby\'s first ear-piercing ceremony to a bride\'s elaborate jhumkas. The right pair of gold earrings frames your face, elevates your outfit, and carries cultural meaning. Let us explore the designs dominating 2026.</p><h2>Classic Earring Styles That Never Go Out of Fashion</h2><h3>Jhumkas (₹12,000 - ₹60,000)</h3><p>The quintessential Indian earring. Bell-shaped with dangling beads or chains, jhumkas come in countless variations — Rajasthani lac jhumkas, Hyderabadi pearl jhumkas, and South Indian temple jhumkas. They are the go-to choice for weddings, festivals, and ethnic wear. Modern lightweight jhumkas (3-6 grams) are comfortable enough for all-day wear.</p><h3>Gold Studs (₹5,000 - ₹25,000)</h3><p>Simple, elegant, and perfect for daily wear. A pair of gold studs is the most versatile jewellery investment you can make. From tiny 2mm balls to ornate floral designs, studs suit every age and face shape. They work equally well with a business suit and a silk saree.</p><h3>Gold Hoops (₹8,000 - ₹30,000)</h3><p>Hoops have made a massive comeback. Small huggie hoops (12-15mm) are perfect for the office, while large hoops (30-50mm) make a bold fashion statement. Twisted, hammered, and diamond-cut finishes add texture and sparkle. Gold hoops suit round and oval face shapes particularly well.</p><h3>Chandbalis (₹18,000 - ₹75,000)</h3><p>Crescent moon-shaped earrings popularised by Bollywood. Chandbalis feature elaborate filigree, kundan, or meenakari work within the crescent frame. They are dramatic, festive, and photograph beautifully. Ideal for sangeet, reception, and Diwali celebrations.</p><h2>Choosing Earrings for Your Face Shape</h2><ul><li><strong>Round face:</strong> Long, dangly earrings like jhumkas and chandbalis elongate the face. Avoid round studs and hoops.</li><li><strong>Oval face:</strong> Lucky you — almost every style works. Experiment freely with studs, hoops, and drops.</li><li><strong>Square face:</strong> Rounded earrings like hoops and teardrop designs soften angular features.</li><li><strong>Heart-shaped face:</strong> Chandelier and drop earrings balance a wider forehead. Avoid heavy tops and wide studs.</li></ul><h2>Lightweight Gold Earrings: The 2026 Trend</h2><p>The biggest trend in gold earrings this year is lightweight comfort. Women want the look of heavy traditional earrings without the earlobe strain. Jewellers are responding with hollow construction, laser-cut designs, and thin sheet work that creates volume without weight. You can now get jhumkas that look like 15-gram pieces but weigh just 5-6 grams.</p><h2>Earring Care Tips</h2><p>Gold earrings are durable but benefit from basic care:</p><ul><li>Clean with warm soapy water and a soft brush monthly</li><li>Remove before swimming — chlorine can discolour gold alloys</li><li>Store each pair separately to prevent scratching</li><li>Check earring backs regularly — loose backs lead to lost earrings</li><li>For heavy earrings, use ear support patches to prevent earlobe stretching</li></ul><blockquote>The right pair of gold earrings can transform your entire look in seconds. Whether you prefer the timeless elegance of studs or the drama of chandbalis, invest in pieces that make you feel beautiful. Discover our earring collection at Trendimus.</blockquote>',
                'is_published'   => true,
