            [
                'title'          => 'Gold Bangles: Traditional Designs, Daily Wear Sets & Price Guide for 2026',
                'slug'           => 'gold-bangles-traditional-designs-price-guide',
                'category'       => 'Bangles & Bracelets',
                'tags'           => ['gold bangles', 'gold bangle designs', 'daily wear gold bangles', 'gold bangle price', 'traditional gold bangles', '22K gold bangles', 'gold kangan'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-gold-bangles.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'Gold bangles are a symbol of prosperity and tradition in Indian culture. This guide covers the most popular bangle designs, how to choose the right size, and what to expect in terms of pricing for 22K gold bangles.',
                'content'        => '<h2>The Timeless Appeal of Gold Bangles</h2><p>In Indian culture, gold bangles are much more than accessories. They symbolise prosperity, marital status, and feminine grace. The gentle clink of gold bangles is a sound deeply embedded in Indian tradition — from a new bride\'s chooda ceremony to a grandmother\'s treasured collection passed down through generations. Gold bangles remain one of the most popular jewellery purchases in India.</p><h2>Types of Gold Bangles</h2><h3>Solid Gold Bangles (₹25,000 - ₹1,50,000 per piece)</h3><p>Solid round bangles are the classic choice. They are weighty, durable, and retain their shape for decades. Available in plain polished finish, diamond-cut textures, or with engraved patterns. Solid bangles typically range from 8-25 grams each. A set of 2 or 4 is the traditional way to wear them.</p><h3>Hollow / Lightweight Bangles (₹12,000 - ₹50,000 per piece)</h3><p>Modern manufacturing techniques create bangles that look substantial but weigh 40-60% less than solid equivalents. Ideal for daily wear without the heaviness. These use less gold, making them more affordable while maintaining the visual impact.</p><h3>Kada Bangles (₹30,000 - ₹2,00,000)</h3><p>A single broad, rigid bangle — often elaborately decorated with meenakari, kundan, or gemstone work. Kadas make a powerful style statement and are popular in Rajasthani and Gujarati traditions. Men\'s kadas in plain gold or with rudraksha beads are also very popular.</p><h3>Antique Finish Bangles (₹20,000 - ₹80,000 per piece)</h3><p>Oxidised or matte-finish gold bangles with a vintage look. Temple designs, Lakshmi motifs, and peacock patterns are carved into the surface. These are statement pieces perfect for festivals and traditional occasions.</p><h2>How to Measure Your Bangle Size</h2><p>Getting the right bangle size is crucial for comfort:</p><ol><li>Close your fingers together as if slipping on a bangle</li><li>Measure the widest point of your hand (across the knuckles) with a measuring tape</li><li>Divide by 3.14 (pi) to get your bangle diameter</li><li>Common sizes: 2.2 (small), 2.4 (medium), 2.6 (large), 2.8 (extra large)</li></ol><p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> For rigid kadas, measure slightly loose. For thin bangles worn in sets, a snug fit is fine since they slip over the hand one at a time.</p><h2>Gold Bangle Pricing in 2026</h2><p>Bangle prices depend on weight, purity, and making charges. At current 22K gold rates of approximately ₹6,800 per gram:</p><ul><li><strong>Lightweight pair (2 bangles, 15g total):</strong> ₹1,02,000 + making charges ₹8,000-₹20,000</li><li><strong>Medium pair (2 bangles, 25g total):</strong> ₹1,70,000 + making charges ₹13,000-₹34,000</li><li><strong>Heavy set (4 bangles, 60g total):</strong> ₹4,08,000 + making charges ₹32,000-₹80,000</li></ul><p>Making charges for bangles typically range from 8% for plain designs to 20% for intricate handwork.</p><h2>Daily Wear vs Occasion Bangles</h2><p><strong>For daily wear:</strong> Choose lightweight, smooth-edged bangles in 22K or 18K gold. Avoid sharp engravings that can scratch skin. 2 or 4 thin bangles are comfortable for all-day wear including office work.</p><p><strong>For occasions:</strong> Go heavier with detailed craftsmanship. Antique finish, meenakari, or stone-studded bangles add drama to wedding and festival outfits. These are investment pieces meant to be treasured and worn on special days.</p><blockquote>Gold bangles are an investment in both beauty and tradition. Whether you prefer the simplicity of plain gold or the grandeur of temple designs, choose pieces that bring you joy every time you wear them. Explore our bangle collection at Trendimus.</blockquote>',
                'is_published'   => true,
