            [
                'title'          => 'Diamond Engagement Rings: How to Choose the Perfect Ring in India (2026)',
                'slug'           => 'diamond-engagement-rings-guide-india',
                'category'       => 'Rings',
                'tags'           => ['diamond ring', 'engagement ring', 'diamond engagement ring', 'solitaire ring', 'diamond ring price india', 'lab grown diamond ring', 'proposal ring'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-diamond-ring.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'Buying a diamond engagement ring is one of the most important jewellery purchases you will ever make. This guide walks you through diamond shapes, settings, budgeting, and the best places to buy engagement rings in India.',
                'content'        => '<h2>The Diamond Engagement Ring: A Modern Indian Tradition</h2><p>While gold rings have been part of Indian weddings for centuries, diamond engagement rings have become equally popular over the past two decades. Whether you are planning a surprise proposal or shopping together as a couple, choosing the right diamond ring is both exciting and overwhelming. This guide simplifies the process so you can focus on the moment, not the stress.</p><h2>Popular Diamond Ring Styles</h2><h3>Solitaire Rings</h3><p>A single diamond on a plain gold or platinum band. The solitaire is the most classic and timeless engagement ring style. The diamond is the star — no distractions. Solitaires range from 0.30 carat (subtle and elegant, ₹40,000-₹70,000) to 1 carat and above (showstopping, ₹2,50,000+). The four-prong and six-prong settings are most popular.</p><h3>Halo Rings</h3><p>A centre diamond surrounded by a ring of smaller diamonds. The halo makes the centre stone appear 20-30% larger and adds incredible sparkle. This is the best choice if you want maximum visual impact on a moderate budget. A 0.50-carat centre stone with a halo looks as impressive as a 0.75-carat solitaire at a fraction of the price.</p><h3>Three-Stone Rings</h3><p>Three diamonds representing the past, present, and future. The centre stone is larger, flanked by two smaller stones. Romantic, symbolic, and increasingly popular in India. They offer excellent value as the overall diamond weight is distributed across three stones.</p><h3>Pavé Band Rings</h3><p>Small diamonds set along the entire band, creating a continuous sparkle. The centre stone sits atop a glittering band that catches light from every angle. Pavé bands look stunning in photographs, making them a social media favourite.</p><h2>Understanding Diamond Pricing in India</h2><p>Diamond ring prices depend on the 4Cs (covered in detail in our separate guide), metal choice, and making charges:</p><ul><li><strong>0.30 carat solitaire in 18K gold:</strong> ₹35,000 - ₹65,000</li><li><strong>0.50 carat solitaire in 18K gold:</strong> ₹75,000 - ₹1,50,000</li><li><strong>0.75 carat solitaire in platinum:</strong> ₹1,80,000 - ₹3,50,000</li><li><strong>1.00 carat solitaire in platinum:</strong> ₹3,00,000 - ₹8,00,000+</li></ul><p>Prices vary dramatically based on diamond quality. A high-clarity, excellent-cut diamond costs significantly more than a lower-grade stone of the same carat weight.</p><h3>Lab-Grown Diamonds: The Smart Alternative</h3><p>Lab-grown diamonds are physically, chemically, and optically identical to mined diamonds — but cost 60-80% less. A 1-carat lab-grown diamond ring that would cost ₹3,00,000+ with a natural diamond can be purchased for ₹80,000-₹1,20,000. They are certified by the same labs (IGI, GIA) and are eco-friendly. In 2026, lab-grown diamonds account for nearly 30% of engagement ring sales in Indian metros.</p><h2>Choosing the Right Metal</h2><p><strong>18K White Gold:</strong> Most popular for diamond rings. The white colour enhances diamond sparkle. Affordable and durable. Needs rhodium replating every 2-3 years.<br><strong>Platinum:</strong> Hypoallergenic, naturally white, and does not need replating. More expensive but lasts a lifetime. The prestige choice.<br><strong>18K Yellow Gold:</strong> Classic and warm. Makes the diamond appear slightly warmer. Beautiful with fancy yellow diamonds.<br><strong>18K Rose Gold:</strong> Romantic and trendy. The pink hue is flattering on Indian skin tones.</p><h2>Ring Size Tips</h2><p>The most common mistake is getting the wrong ring size. If it is a surprise proposal, borrow one of her existing rings and trace the inner circle on paper, or press it into a bar of soap. Alternatively, ask her best friend or sister — they usually know. Most jewellers offer one free resizing within the first year.</p><blockquote>An engagement ring is a symbol of your commitment. Focus on what she loves — not what marketing tells you to buy. The best engagement ring is one that makes her smile every time she looks at her hand. Explore our diamond ring collection at Trendimus.</blockquote>',
                'is_published'   => true,
                'published_at'   => now()->subDays(22),
                'view_count'     => 1423,
                'seo_data'       => [
