            [
                'title'          => 'Best Diamond Necklace Designs for Indian Women: Solitaire Pendants to Statement Sets',
                'slug'           => 'best-diamond-necklace-designs-india',
                'category'       => 'Necklaces & Pendants',
                'tags'           => ['diamond necklace', 'diamond pendant', 'solitaire pendant', 'diamond necklace designs', 'diamond jewellery india', 'diamond choker', 'diamond necklace price'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-diamond-necklace.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'Diamond necklaces range from delicate solitaire pendants for daily wear to grand chokers for weddings. Discover the best diamond necklace designs for Indian women and how to choose one that suits your lifestyle and budget.',
                'content'        => '<h2>Diamond Necklaces: From Everyday Elegance to Wedding Grandeur</h2><p>A diamond necklace elevates every outfit instantly. Whether it is a tiny solitaire pendant peeking out from a kurta neckline or a cascading diamond choker at a wedding reception, diamonds around the neck have an unmatched allure. The Indian diamond jewellery market has evolved tremendously, offering designs that bridge traditional and contemporary aesthetics beautifully.</p><h2>Diamond Necklace Styles</h2><h3>Solitaire Pendants (₹25,000 - ₹1,50,000)</h3><p>A single diamond on a delicate chain — the most popular diamond necklace purchase in India. Solitaire pendants are perfect for daily wear because they are subtle yet unmistakably luxurious. A 0.25-0.50 carat pendant in 18K white gold is the sweet spot for most women. It works with office wear, casual outfits, and even formal gowns.</p><h3>Diamond Chokers (₹1,50,000 - ₹8,00,000+)</h3><p>Sitting snugly at the base of the neck, diamond chokers are a bridal favourite. They come in single-line designs for understated elegance or multi-row cascading patterns for full bridal drama. Polki diamond chokers with uncut stones give a traditional Mughal aesthetic, while brilliant-cut diamond chokers are sleek and modern.</p><h3>Rivière Necklaces (₹2,00,000 - ₹10,00,000+)</h3><p>A continuous line of individually set diamonds, graduated in size from the clasp to the centre. Also called a tennis necklace or eternity necklace. This is the epitome of diamond luxury — understated but unmissable. Often chosen for milestone anniversaries or as heirloom pieces.</p><h3>Diamond Mangalsutra (₹30,000 - ₹1,50,000)</h3><p>The modern Indian woman wants a mangalsutra that doubles as a fashion accessory. Diamond mangalsutras feature a diamond pendant on a black bead chain, often in 18K gold. They are sleek enough for the office and meaningful enough for tradition. This is one of the fastest-growing diamond jewellery categories in India.</p><h2>Choosing the Right Diamond Necklace</h2><p><strong>For daily wear:</strong> Solitaire pendants or small diamond clusters on fine chains. Choose 18K white gold for durability. Budget ₹25,000-₹75,000.</p><p><strong>For office and parties:</strong> Diamond bar pendants, initial pendants with diamond accents, or a classic tennis necklace. These transition effortlessly from day to night. Budget ₹50,000-₹2,00,000.</p><p><strong>For weddings and bridal:</strong> Diamond chokers, layered sets, or polki necklaces. These are statement pieces designed to be photographed and remembered. Budget ₹2,00,000 and above.</p><h2>Caring for Your Diamond Necklace</h2><ul><li>Store separately in a soft pouch — diamonds can scratch other jewellery and even other diamonds</li><li>Clean monthly with warm water, mild soap, and a soft toothbrush</li><li>Avoid wearing during cooking — grease dulls diamond sparkle</li><li>Get prong settings checked annually by a jeweller to prevent loose stones</li><li>Remove before applying perfume, sunscreen, or hairspray</li></ul><blockquote>A diamond necklace is an investment that appreciates — both in value and in the joy it brings. Start with a solitaire pendant and build your collection over time. Explore diamond necklaces at Trendimus.</blockquote>',
                'is_published'   => true,
                'published_at'   => now()->subDays(20),
                'view_count'     => 876,
