            [
                'title'          => 'Wedding Ring Guide for Couples: Gold, Platinum & Diamond Bands in India (2026)',
                'slug'           => 'wedding-ring-guide-couples-gold-platinum-diamond',
                'category'       => 'Rings',
                'tags'           => ['wedding rings', 'couple rings', 'wedding band', 'platinum wedding ring', 'gold wedding ring', 'diamond wedding band', 'couple ring designs', 'engagement band'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-wedding-rings.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'Choosing wedding rings as a couple is a special milestone. This guide covers matching couple rings, metal options (gold vs platinum), diamond bands, and how to find the perfect wedding rings that symbolise your bond.',
                'content'        => '<h2>Wedding Rings: The Jewellery You Will Never Take Off</h2><p>Your wedding ring is arguably the most significant piece of jewellery you will ever own. It is the one piece you will wear every single day for the rest of your life — through work, travel, celebrations, and quiet moments. Choosing the right wedding ring as a couple deserves careful thought about comfort, durability, style, and budget.</p><h2>Metal Options for Wedding Rings</h2><h3>22K Gold (₹15,000 - ₹40,000 per ring)</h3><p>The traditional Indian choice. Rich yellow colour, auspicious significance, and excellent resale value. 22K gold is softer than other options, so plain bands may show scratches over years of daily wear. Best for couples who prefer traditional aesthetics and value gold as an investment.</p><h3>18K Gold (₹12,000 - ₹35,000 per ring)</h3><p>Harder and more durable than 22K. Available in yellow, white, and rose gold. White gold wedding bands have a platinum-like appearance at a lower price. Rose gold bands have a warm, romantic hue that is increasingly popular. 18K gold is the best balance of beauty, durability, and value for wedding rings.</p><h3>Platinum (₹25,000 - ₹80,000 per ring)</h3><p>The premium choice. Platinum is naturally white, hypoallergenic, and incredibly durable. It does not wear away — it merely develops a patina that can be polished. Platinum rings are heavier, which gives them a substantial, luxurious feel on the finger. The higher price reflects rarity and density.</p><h2>Popular Wedding Ring Styles for Couples</h2><h3>Matching Bands</h3><p>Identical or complementary designs for him and her. His band is typically wider (5-6mm) while hers is narrower (3-4mm). Matching rings symbolise unity and look cohesive in photographs. Engraving each other\'s names or wedding date on the inner surface adds a hidden personal touch.</p><h3>Diamond Bands</h3><p>Her ring features diamonds — channel-set, pavé-set, or a single centre stone — while his remains plain or has a subtle diamond accent. Diamond wedding bands sparkle alongside engagement rings and catch light beautifully. A half-eternity band (diamonds around half the ring) is the most practical choice as it allows for future resizing.</p><h3>Two-Tone Bands</h3><p>Combining two metals — white and yellow gold, or platinum and rose gold — in a single ring. The contrast creates a distinctive look that is modern and eye-catching. Two-tone rings are perfect for couples who want something unique without going too unconventional.</p><h2>Comfort Fit vs Standard Fit</h2><p>This is the most overlooked factor in wedding ring selection:</p><ul><li><strong>Standard fit:</strong> Flat inner surface. Traditional. Slightly harder to put on and take off.</li><li><strong>Comfort fit:</strong> Rounded inner surface. Slides on easily and feels like nothing on your finger. We strongly recommend comfort fit for rings you will wear 24/7.</li></ul><p>Most jewellers offer comfort fit at the same price. If they charge extra, the small premium is absolutely worth it for a lifetime of daily wear.</p><h2>Ring Sizing Tips for Couples</h2><ul><li>Get sized at the end of the day when fingers are slightly swollen — this is their maximum size</li><li>Temperature affects ring size — fingers are thinner in cold weather and slightly larger in heat</li><li>Wide bands (6mm+) should be sized half a size larger than narrow bands</li><li>If knuckles are significantly larger than the finger base, choose a size that slides over knuckles comfortably</li><li>Many couples have their rings sized together at the jeweller for accuracy</li></ul><h2>Wedding Ring Budget Guide</h2><p>Budget both rings together as a set:</p><ul><li><strong>Budget (both rings):</strong> ₹20,000 - ₹50,000 — 18K gold plain bands</li><li><strong>Mid-range (both rings):</strong> ₹50,000 - ₹1,50,000 — Platinum or diamond-accented bands</li><li><strong>Premium (both rings):</strong> ₹1,50,000 - ₹3,00,000+ — Platinum with diamonds, designer brands</li></ul><blockquote>Your wedding rings do not need to be the most expensive jewellery you own — they need to be the most meaningful. Choose rings that feel right on your fingers and right for your bond. Explore couple wedding rings at Trendimus.</blockquote>',
                'is_published'   => true,
                'published_at'   => now()->subDays(6),
                'view_count'     => 943,
                'seo_data'       => [
                    'meta_title'       => 'Wedding Ring Guide: Gold, Platinum & Diamond Bands India (2026) | Trendimus',
                    'meta_description' => 'Complete wedding ring guide for Indian couples. Gold vs platinum vs diamond bands. Matching couple ring designs, sizing tips, comfort fit & budget guide.',
                ],
